---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Book",
  name: "The Ritz London: The Cookbook",
  author: { "@type": "Person", name: "John Williams" },
  publisher: "Mitchell Beazley",
  datePublished: "2018",
  numberOfPages: 240,
  isbn: "9781784724962",
  description:
    "The Ritz London's first cookbook: 100 fine-dining recipes from the hotel's dining rooms, arranged by season.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Ritz London Cookbook (2026 Guide) — Recipes, Price & Where to Buy"
  description="Guide to The Ritz London cookbook by John Williams MBE: 100 recipes from the Ritz Restaurant, Palm Court and Rivoli Bar, Mitchell Beazley 2018, £30 at the official Ritz shop."
  path="/the-ritz-london-cookbook/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Guide · The Ritz London · Cookbook
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      The Ritz London Cookbook
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Can't get a table — or want to cook like the kitchen? <strong>The Ritz London:
      The Cookbook</strong> is the hotel's first recipe book, by Executive Chef
      <strong>John Williams MBE</strong> (in the Ritz kitchen since 2004). This page
      covers what's inside, the price, and where to buy it — from official sources.
    </p>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>The facts</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Title:</strong> The Ritz London: The Cookbook</li>
        <li><strong>Author:</strong> John Williams MBE, Executive Chef of The Ritz London</li>
        <li><strong>Publisher:</strong> Mitchell Beazley (Hachette UK), 2018</li>
        <li><strong>Format:</strong> hardcover, 240 pages, ISBN 9781784724962</li>
        <li><strong>Price:</strong> £30.00 at the official Ritz online shop (checked October 2026)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What's inside</h2>
      <p>
        The book presents <strong>100 fine-dining recipes</strong> served across the
        hotel's dining rooms — The Ritz Restaurant, the Palm Court, and the Rivoli Bar
        (official Ritz shop page). The recipes are arranged in <strong>four seasonal
        chapters</strong> — spring, summer, autumn, winter — and each season opens with a
        creative cocktail-and-canapé pairing, followed by breakfasts and first courses,
        mains, and desserts. In our own summary: it is the closest you can get to the
        Ritz kitchen at home, written by the chef who has run it for two decades.
      </p>

      <h2>Where to buy</h2>
      <p>
        The official Ritz online gift shop sells it under "Culinary" — buying direct
        supports the hotel. It is also stocked by major booksellers (Waterstones,
        Amazon UK) — prices there vary, so compare before you buy.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.theritzlondon.com/product/the-ritz-london-cookbook/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official Ritz shop — The Ritz London Cookbook (£30.00)</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Worth knowing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>First of its kind:</strong> published in 2018, it was the hotel's first-ever recipe book.</li>
        <li><strong>Fine-dining level:</strong> these are restaurant recipes — expect Escoffier technique, long ingredient lists, and serious ambition rather than weeknight cooking.</li>
        <li><strong>Not a menu:</strong> for current restaurant prices and menus, see our <a href="/the-ritz-restaurant-menu/">restaurant menu guide</a> and <a href="/ritz-menu-prices/">price guide</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Official links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.theritzlondon.com/product/the-ritz-london-cookbook/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Ritz London Cookbook — official Ritz shop</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.theritzlondon.com/dine-with-us/the-ritz-restaurant/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Ritz Restaurant — official page</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About this guide</p>
      <p>
        This is an independent guide and is not affiliated with The Ritz London.
        Book details come from the official Ritz shop page and the publisher's listing
        (Hachette UK), checked October 2026. Prices and availability change — verify
        with the retailer before buying.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related guides -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">More Ritz guides</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/the-ritz-restaurant-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">The Ritz Restaurant menu</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— full menu summary with official prices</span></li>
        <li><a href="/ritz-menu-prices/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Menu prices — what dinner really costs</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— realistic totals with service charge</span></li>
        <li><a href="/ritz-afternoon-tea/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Afternoon tea at the Palm Court</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— from £95 per adult</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
